### authentication-service — example requests
# authentication/authentication-service-with-loco — the central SSO
# provider (not an entity registry). Envelope: BARE loco JSON — a
# success body is the payload itself, no wrapper; non-2xx is loco's own
# {"error":"...","description":"..."} (or, for the always-200 signup/
# magic-link endpoints, `{}`). See 00-auth-handshake.http for the full
# walkthrough with inline curl-verified commentary on retrieving a
# magic-link token in this compose (LOCO_ENV=production is baked into
# the image — SEC-A1 fail-closed — so the usual "read it from the dev
# console log" trick needs a throwaway container overridden to
# LOCO_ENV=development; see that file). This file is the flatter
# per-endpoint reference; run 00-auth-handshake.http first if you want
# working values for @sessionCookie / @csrfToken / @token / @pid below.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8091
@email = demo@example.com
@magicLinkToken = REPLACE_WITH_TOKEN_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http
@sessionCookie = REPLACE_WITH_SESSION_COOKIE
@csrfToken = REPLACE_WITH_CSRF_COOKIE_VALUE
@token = REPLACE_WITH_BEARER_FROM_00-auth-handshake.http
@pid = REPLACE_WITH_PID_FROM_VERIFY_RESPONSE


### Health check
GET {{baseUrl}}/_health


### Sign up — creates the account (if new) and issues a magic link.
# Always 200 {} — deliberate anti-enumeration (SEC-A5/A6), never reveals
# whether the email was new, existing, or rate-limited.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signup
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "name": "Demo User" }


### Re-request a magic link for an existing account (sign-in). Same
# always-200-{} contract as signup.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/magic-link
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}" }


### Verify the magic link — GET, token in the path, no body.
# curl-verified live (00-auth-handshake.http): 200 with LoginResponse
# {"token","pid","name","email","is_verified"} + two Set-Cookie headers
# (__Host-mxi_session HttpOnly, __Host-mxi_csrf readable).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/magic-link/{{magicLinkToken}}


### Exchange the session for a short-lived PASETO v4.public token.
# Requires both the session cookie and the matching CSRF header.
# curl-verified: 200 {"token":"v4.public...."}.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/token
Cookie: __Host-mxi_session={{sessionCookie}}
X-CSRF-Token: {{csrfToken}}


### Who am I — session + bearer introspection.
# curl-verified: {"pid","name","email"}.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/me
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accepts-version: 1.0


### The published Ed25519 key set every peer verifies against (public,
# no auth). curl-verified shape: {"keys":[{"kty":"OKP","crv":"Ed25519",
# "kid","use":"sig","x"}]}.
GET {{baseUrl}}/.well-known/paseto-keys


### GDPR export of the caller's own account — curl-verified shape:
# {"user":{...},"sessions":[...],"auth_events":[...]}.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/account/export
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### The caller's own auth event history — curl-verified: an array of
# {event,email,user_pid,detail,created_at} (e.g. "signup",
# "magic_link_redeemed").
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/account/audit
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Admin — system-wide recent audit log. Requires `attrs.access` to
# include "admin"; curl-verified: 403 without it (the bootstrap admin is
# assigned via the `user_attributes` CLI task, not HTTP — see §9/§10
# below).
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/audit/recent
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Admin — list a user's ABAC attributes (attrs claim source,
# agents/share/authorization-attributes.md §6). Expect 403 unless
# you've bootstrapped an admin locally.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/admin/users/{{pid}}/attributes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Admin — replace a user's ABAC attributes (full replacement, not a
# merge; revokes all of the target user's sessions on success).
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/admin/users/{{pid}}/attributes
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "attributes": { "access": ["write"], "dept": ["cardiology"] } }


### Sign out — clears both cookies, revokes the session.
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/signout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}


### Delete the caller's own account (GDPR erasure)
# DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/auth/account
# Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
